<title>SINGAPORE: IOC sells Madras low aromatic naphtha to Hanwha.</title>
<headline>IOC sells Madras low aromatic naphtha to Hanwha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) to South Korea's Hanwha Chemical Corp at $14.48 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the cargo is for lifting January 1-3 free-on-board (fob) Madras on the east coast.</p>
<p>The tender closed December 12 and was valid until December 13.</p>
<p>Hanwha also won IOC's last LAN cargo, 25,000 tonnes from Visag on the east coast, lifting December 15-17, at $14.87 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.  </p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
